usage: walmart-collector [-h] [--version] [--config CONFIG] [--pretty]
                         {validate-config,db-upgrade,sync-config,run,resume,finalize,replay,stop,publish,status,export,validate-export,provider-balance,set-ceiling,set-budget,coverage-report,follow-ups,schedule-status,field-dispositions,import-detail-captures,attest-lineage,release-hold,schedule-info,ops}
                         ...

``walmart-collector``: the headless collector's command line.

positional arguments:
  {validate-config,db-upgrade,sync-config,run,resume,finalize,replay,stop,publish,status,export,validate-export,provider-balance,set-ceiling,set-budget,coverage-report,follow-ups,schedule-status,field-dispositions,import-detail-captures,attest-lineage,release-hold,schedule-info,ops}
    validate-config     check the configuration files and the environment
    db-upgrade          create or upgrade the database schema
    sync-config         load the stores and the category CSV into the database
    run                 collect a store (a new run)
    resume              continue an interrupted run from its checkpoints
    finalize            check and export what an unfinished run collected (no
                        provider request)
    replay              read an earlier live run's stored pages again with
                        this code (offline; a REPLAY run, never published)
    stop                stop collecting; the run is finalized with what it
                        collected
    publish             publish a complete validated run
    status              runs, holds, the published dataset and the provider
                        ledger
    export              copy a run's verified export files to a folder
    validate-export     the 22-field contract (and, for a run, the source
                        check)
    provider-balance    the provider's balance (Scrape.do: free /info) or, for
                        Oxylabs, its ceiling and ledger
    set-ceiling         a provider's spending ceiling across every run from
                        now on
    set-budget          the task's money budget across every provider from now
                        on
    coverage-report     a run's coverage reconciliation and follow-up outcomes
    follow-ups          the store's follow-up queue: sponsored-only products
                        and variant siblings its runs named, and whether a run
                        has read them to a decision
    schedule-status     the store's scheduled occurrences: backlog, lateness,
                        missed deadlines and the capacity gap (reads only)
    field-dispositions  why each exported product's UPC and size are filled or
                        empty, in a run (reads only)
    import-detail-captures
                        load saved product pages, with their original time,
                        run, revision and hash, for runs to reuse (offline: no
                        provider request; pages of another item are refused)
    attest-lineage      record that a LIVE run made before release 1.3.1 read
                        its pages from the network (its observations may then
                        serve later runs)
    release-hold        let a held store collect again
    schedule-info       the store's schedule and the Azure cron expression
                        (UTC)
    ops                 run the command written in $WALMART_COLLECTOR_COMMAND
                        (the Azure operations job; default: status)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  --config CONFIG       collector configuration file (default:
                        $WALMART_COLLECTOR_CONFIG or config/collector.yaml)
  --pretty              print the result indented
